se* to call zero. We could have called 5 the origin, and everything would still work, just with different numbers. The universe has no "chosen" origin point. The Big Bang is the *temporal* origin (the beginning of time), but it is not a *spatial* origin. Every point in the universe is equally "original." ### A Final, Simple Analogy Imagine a perfectly smooth, infinite rubber sheet. There are no marks on it. - **You ask:** "Where is the center of this sheet?" - **The answer:** "There is no center. Every point is the same as every other point." - **You ask:** "But what if I put a dot on it? Isn't that the center now?" - **The answer:** "No. The dot is just a dot. You can call it the center if you want, but that's a choice you made. The sheet itself still has no center." GPS is like putting a dot on the sheet (the Earth) and building a map around that dot. It works perfectly for navigating *on the dot*. But it tells you nothing about the sheet itself. The universe is the sheet. It has no center. And GPS, for all its brilliance, is just a map of a tiny dot on that sheet.
